      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "μάλιστα δὲ ἐὰν ἐμπέσῃ εἰς αὐτὴν δοῦλος Θεοῦ καὶ μὴ ᾖ συνετός, δαπανᾶται ὑπ’ αὐτῆς δεινῶς.",
          "english_quote": "If a servant of God[c] falls into it and is not sensible, it consumes him terribly.",
          "issue": "The conditional and negation are preserved, but μάλιστα, “especially,” is omitted. This removes the source’s explicit emphasis linking this particular case to the preceding general assertion about consumption.",
          "suggested_revision": "For fresh review: “This is especially so if a servant of God[c] falls into it and is not sensible: it consumes him terribly.”",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "Ἄκουσον, [φησίν,] ἐν ποίοις ἔργοις θανατοῖ ἡ ἐπιθυμία ἡ πονηρὰ τοὺς δούλους τοῦ Θεοῦ.",
          "english_quote": "Bounded Athos and Latin alternatives are separately disclosed in reader notes.",
          "issue": "Independently of the standard edition, this edition also claims reader-facing disclosure of Athos and Latin alternatives that its supplied notes do not actually present.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the claim or supply the specific alternatives with their provenance. Do not substitute an undisclosed variant for the selected working text.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "Ἄκουσον, [φησίν,]",
          "english_quote": "The working i.3 brackets he says; the 1891 apparatus calls it Harmer’s insertion supported by versions, while Lake (1907) Plate VIII lacks it. The English supplies the disclosed working attribution, not a claim of unanimous Greek.",
          "issue": "The brackets and editorial status are disclosed correctly, but the categorical apparatus and plate claims cannot be established from the supplied working transcription. Reusing the standard note does not independently substantiate them.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep the bracketed-attribution disclosure. Provide supporting apparatus and witness evidence for the historical claims, or qualify them as unverified reports. No change to the included speaker attribution is required merely because an alternative is reported.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The standard main text covers the selected Greek faithfully, including its conditions, negations, death assertions, and disclosed bracketed attribution. The simplified text additionally loses the explicit “especially” emphasis. Both editions require correction of unsupported or absent alternative-disclosure claims. Reader-facing “servant” follows current policy. This review assesses the supplied working transcription and English materials, not unseen editions, manuscript handwriting, or exhaustive collation; proposed wording still requires fresh review."
